course: dictionary
lesson: 13247
title: Getting: many meanings in one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One small word can have many meanings, so you need the context to know which one the writer means. «I'm getting a new bike.» Here getting means receiving: the bike is coming to me. Ask yourself what the sentence is about before you choose a meaning.
explain: «It's getting dark.» Getting does not mean receiving here, because you cannot receive darkness. It means becoming: the sky is changing into dark. Try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: «Are you getting this?» means «Do you understand?» Phrases change the meaning too. Getting up means rising from bed, and getting dressed means putting on your clothes. Two words together can mean something different from each word on its own.
fact: Getting is the -ing form of the verb get (get, gets, got, getting).
fact: «Getting» can mean receiving, becoming, arriving, understanding or fetching.
fact: When «getting» is followed by a word like cold, better or older, it usually means becoming.
fact: Phrases such as «getting up», «getting ready» and «getting along» have their own meanings.
fact: A good check is to swap in another meaning, such as becoming, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «I'm getting a new bike for my birthday.» What does getting mean here? | *Receiving | Becoming | Understanding | Arriving
exercise: «It's getting dark outside.» What does getting mean here? | Fetching | Understanding | *Becoming | Receiving
exercise: «Are you getting this?» What does it mean? | Are you arriving home? | Are you fetching it? | *Do you understand? | Are you receiving a parcel?
test: «She is getting the milk from the fridge.» What does getting mean here? | Understanding | Receiving | *Fetching | Becoming
test: «Jo is getting better after her cold.» What does getting mean here? | Fetching | *Becoming | Arriving | Receiving
exam: «We are getting up early for the trip.» What does getting up mean? | *Rising from bed | Arriving at school | Lying down to sleep | Receiving a present
